WEBVTT

00:23:26.995 --> 00:23:31.073
And so, isn't it possible
that once we train humans,

00:23:31.097 --> 00:23:33.215
they can beat the algorithm?

00:23:34.071 --> 00:23:35.615
CM: Yeah, it's always possible.

00:23:35.639 --> 00:23:38.518
You're making their judgment
more algorithmic, which is good.

00:23:38.542 --> 00:23:39.932
A hundred percent support it.

00:23:39.956 --> 00:23:41.124
AG: I guess, though,

00:23:41.148 --> 00:23:42.892
I worry about another piece of this.

00:23:42.916 --> 00:23:45.662
If we're using algorithms
to predict people's performance,

00:23:45.686 --> 00:23:49.041
we're almost exclusively relying
on individual performance data.

00:23:49.065 --> 00:23:50.472
There's still a huge problem,

00:23:50.496 --> 00:23:52.941
which is, you're getting
an individual superstar

00:23:52.965 --> 00:23:56.069
who might just destroy
the people around that person.

00:23:56.093 --> 00:23:58.004
You might hire somebody who's a genius,

00:23:58.028 --> 00:23:59.416
but toxic to the culture.

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:01.416
I want to get people who elevate a team,